<article class="env-lemma" id="0FH8">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FH8">Lemma <span data-tag="0FH8">45.8.4</span>.</a> Let $K/k$ be an algebraic extension of fields. Let $X$ be a finite type scheme over $k$. The kernel of the map $\mathop{\mathrm{CH}}\nolimits _ i(X) \to \mathop{\mathrm{CH}}\nolimits _ i(X_ K)$ constructed in Lemma <a href="/tag/0FH6" data-tag="0FH6">45.8.2</a> is torsion. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      It clearly suffices to show that the kernel of flat pullback $\mathop{\mathrm{CH}}\nolimits _ i(X) \to \mathop{\mathrm{CH}}\nolimits _ i(X_{k'})$ by $\pi : X_{k'} \to X$ is torsion for any finite extension $k'/k$. This is clear because $\pi _* \pi ^* \alpha = [k' : k] \alpha $ by Chow Homology, Lemma <a href="/tag/02RH" data-tag="02RH">42.15.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>